      </bf:SupplementaryContent>
    </bf:supplementaryContent>
    <bf:summary>
      <bf:Summary>
	<rdfs:label>"This book examines the fundamental properties, synthesis strategies, and applications of two-dimensional quantum materials in energy technologies. It highlights their potential for transforming energy storage, conversion, and harvesting systems. Bridging the gap between theoretical foundations and practical implementation, the book demonstrates their role in advancing next-generation energy solutions, including photovoltaics, thermoelectrics, fuel cells, and energy storage devices such as supercapacitors and batteries. Features: Explores the unique properties and applications of 2D quantum materials. Adopts an interdisciplinary approach to quantum energy technologies by integrating physics, materials science, and energy engineering. Includes recent advancements and emerging trends, such as the use of 2D materials with artificial intelligence for material discovery and sustainability assessments. Emphasizes practical applications in solar cells, batteries, and energy storage systems. Examines real-world case studies and examples to simplify complex quantum concepts. This book is intended for researchers, engineers, and students in materials science, nanotechnology, quantum technology and energy engineering, supporting innovation in sustainable energy solutions"-- Provided by publisher.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:Summary>
    </bf:summary>
    <bf:tableOfContents>
      <bf:TableOfContents>
	<rdfs:label>Introduction to two-dimensional quantum materials / Abdus Salam Sarkar, Emmanuel Stratakis -- Synthesis and advanced characterization techniques / Yu-Chi Lee, Yu-Chuan Lin -- Electronic, magnetic, topological and optical properties / Yusheng Hou, Ruqian Wu -- Photophysics and excited-state dynamics of 2D quantum materials for energy conversion / Nagendra S. Kamath, Ashish Soni, Abdus Salam Sarkar, Suman Kalyan Pal -- Exciton dynamics in 2D quantum material heterostructures / Junyuan Lu, Austin Yin, Jingang Li -- Two-dimensional quantum materials for next-generation photovoltaics / Arul Varman Kesavan, Dheebanathan Azhakanantham, Muthamizh Selvamani, Praveen C. Ramamurthy -- Thermoelectrics in 2D quantum materials : Harnessing waste heat / Shamim Sk -- Piezoelectric and triboelectric nanogenerators : Energy harvesting applications / Naoki Higashitarumizu -- 2D quantum materials : Photodetectors and optoelectronic devices / Amer Abdulghani, Dinelka Somaweera, Ishara Umayangani Weerasinghe Muthugalage, Andergachew Mekonnen Berhe, Andrey E. Miroshnichenko, Haroldo T. Hattori -- 2D quantum materials : Spin optoelectronics, topological effects and their potential energy applications / Murli Kumar Manglam, Binoy Krishna Hazra -- 2D quantum materials for batteries : Lithium-ion, sodium-ion and beyond / Sayan Maji, Subahm Ghosh, Urmimala Maitra -- Two-dimensional quantum materials for energy storage supercapacitor devices / Priyadarshani Tamang, Rumana Sultana Parvin, Sk Riyajuddin -- Spin-valley polarization in transition metal dichalcogenides and applications / Eirini Katsipoulaki, Emmanouel Stratakis, George Kioseoglou -- Hybrid and heterostructure of 2D quantum materials / Yingying Wu -- Perspectives on 2D quantum materials for energy applications / Abdus Salam Sarkar, Emmanuel Stratakis.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:TableOfContents>
    </bf:tableOfContents>
